+## 🖥️ Restricting screen share to the hosts
+
+By default every token allows publishing every source. With `LIVEKIT_RESTRICT_SCREEN_SHARE=true` the tokens of
+`/sfu/get`, `/get_token` and the proxied `get_token` carry `canPublishSources` (which supersedes `canPublish` at the
+SFU):
+
+- power level of the user at or above the room's `kick` level (default 50): `camera`, `microphone`, `screen_share`,
+  `screen_share_audio`;
+- anybody else, and any case in which the power cannot be read: `camera`, `microphone`.
+
+The power is read once per token, as the user (application service masquerading with the AS token), from
+`m.room.power_levels` (`users[user]`, else `users_default`, default 0). Without a power levels event the creator has
+100 (`m.room.create`, `creator`); in room version 12 the creators (the sender of the create event and
+`additional_creators`) are above every level. The read has a 3 second limit. Every failure (timeout, error status,
+unparseable or malformed content, a user of another homeserver) gives camera and microphone only; the token request
+itself still succeeds. Users without publish rights (restricted access) and federated users relayed through the
+federation proxy are unchanged. The flag needs the application service configuration, whose `users` namespace covers
+the local users.
+
